--- schema: workflow-plan/1.2 source: ./source.md strategy: systematic depth: standard slug: TASK-WF-makeTheAliasOnly-20261105-051649 version: "1" priority: Medium created_date: "2026-11-05" --- # Make alias-only model selection explicit and tested (#384, option A), revised after review Source: ./source.md Goal: Agents, commands, skills and the Python package select models only through the plain aliases opus, sonnet and haiku; a test with a documented allow-list enforces it, the sites that bypass the aliases are fixed, and the alias-to-tier mapping (opus to claude-gw-tier1a, sonnet to claude-gw-tier1b, haiku to claude-gw-tier2 inside a ccsession tier workspace once the launcher sets it, nothing set outside) is documented together with the exact spec of the later launcher change and a failing-first test for it. ## Constraints - Do not edit anything under src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/ or any ccsession-orca file (issue #315 owns them); read them only. Do not edit the ccsession launcher in this change. - Agent, command and skill text keeps the plain aliases opus, sonnet and haiku. The three issue-worker agents (src/superclaude/agents/issue-worker-t1.md, issue-worker-t2.md, issue-worker-t3.md) keep their pinned claude-gw-tier ids as documented allow-list exceptions. - Edit under src/ only; the .claude/ copies are gitignored sync output regenerated by make sync-dev. Where an edited src/superclaude file has a byte-identical copy under plugins/superclaude/, copy the edited file over that mirror so both stay identical. - Do not change `model:` values in any agent file, and do not add agent files. - New text that describes the mapping says it holds once the launcher sets the three variables; today the workspace defaults file exports real model ids for them. - New files and edits never spell the retired underscore names of the retry-ladder variables literally (build any pattern from a regex such as T[0-4]_Model), so the Task 5 grep stays clean. - Python commands run through uv (uv run pytest ...). Run only the tests named in a task plus the tests that read the files it edits; never the whole suite and never tests/cli/eval/ as a directory. - Task-owned evidence is written under ./artifacts/ in this package. ## Phase 1: Pin the policy with tests that fail first ## Task 1: Add the alias-only policy tests Create tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py (ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2], like tests/skills/test_issue_worker_agents.py, which also shows how agent frontmatter is parsed). Define ALIASES = opus, sonnet, haiku, inherit and two allow-list constants, each with a one-line reason: ISSUE_WORKER_PINS (the three issue-worker agent files, whose pinned values must equal claude-gw-tier3, claude-gw-tier2 and claude-gw-tier1a; reason: they stop with E-TIER-UNAVAILABLE outside a ccsession tier workspace, see src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/refs/tiers.md) and TIER_TEXT_ALLOWED (those three files, everything under src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/, and src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/ which is read-only here). Tests, each with a docstring naming the rule: - When a `model:` line is present in the frontmatter of a file in src/superclaude/agents/*.md, src/superclaude/skills/*/SKILL.md or src/superclaude/commands/*.md, its value is in ALIASES, except the allow-listed issue workers; files without a `model:` line are skipped. - The text claude-gw-tier appears under src/superclaude/agents, commands, skills, cli, hooks and core only in TIER_TEXT_ALLOWED paths. - No non-docstring string constant in any src/superclaude/**/*.py module, skipping src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/, matches `^claude-(opus|sonnet|haiku|fable)-\d` (parse with ast; comments and docstrings are skipped). A residual allow-list dict (path to reason) exists for any legitimate hit found when the test first runs. - No line of any .md file under src/superclaude/agents, commands or skills (skipping src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/) passes a full model id to a model flag, matched by `--models?[ =]+`?claude-(opus|sonnet|haiku|fable)-\d`. - superclaude.cli.reflect.commands._DEFAULT_MODEL is in ALIASES. - docs/testing/v5.0.0/user/D12-reflect.md does not contain claude-opus-4-8. - The brainstorm steps in src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/refs/chains.md contain no `--models` flag. - src/superclaude/agents/audit-scanner.md pins `model: sonnet`, and no .md file under src/superclaude/skills/sc-cleanup-audit-protocol/ (SKILL.md and templates/) nor src/superclaude/commands/cleanup-audit.md contains the word Haiku. - Neither src/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/refs/retry.md nor refs/ledger.md, nor their copies under plugins/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/refs/, contains a name matching `T[0-4]_Model`, and retry.md names the primary-ladder variables T3Model01, T2Model02, T1Model02 and T1Model01. - docs/reference/model-aliases.md exists and states the three exports with the exact ids ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-gw-tier1a, ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=claude-gw-tier1b, ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-gw-tier2; and tier1a, tier1b and tier2 are keys of "tiers" in src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/ccsession-models.json (read only). Acceptance criteria: - tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py exists and `uv run pytest tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py` run on the unchanged tree fails exactly these seven tests: the Python constants test, the reflect default test, the D12 test, the chains test, the cleanup-audit test, the retry names test and the mapping document test; the remaining tests pass. The pytest output is saved to ./artifacts/t1-red.log. - Every failing test fails for the stated reason (for example the Python constants test reports src/superclaude/cli/reflect/commands.py and claude-opus-4-8), not an import or collection error. - `uv run ruff check tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py` and `uv run ruff format --check tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py` pass. ## Phase 2: Fix the sites that bypass the aliases ## Task 2: Make the reflect default model an alias and update the D12 manual test Depends on: Task 1 In src/superclaude/cli/reflect/commands.py change `_DEFAULT_MODEL = "claude-opus-4-8"` (line 31) to `"opus"` and update the comment above it (lines 26-30) to say the default is the plain alias opus, that ANTHROPIC_MODEL still takes precedence at the use in the reflect run command (`model = os.environ.get("ANTHROPIC_MODEL", "").strip() or _DEFAULT_MODEL`, about line 359), and that the alias maps to a ccsession tier model once the launcher sets ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL (see the model-alias reference page in docs/reference). The comment must not contain the literal tier id. In docs/testing/v5.0.0/user/D12-reflect.md change the expected command at line 235 from `--model claude-opus-4-8` to `--model opus`, and reword line 243 if it describes the old default. Find the tests that import superclaude.cli.reflect.commands or reference _DEFAULT_MODEL (search tests/ for them) and run them. Acceptance criteria: - `grep -n claude-opus-4-8 src/superclaude/cli/reflect/commands.py docs/testing/v5.0.0/user/D12-reflect.md` returns nothing and `_DEFAULT_MODEL == "opus"`. - In tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py the Python constants test, the reflect default test, the D12 test and the claude-gw-tier text test pass; the reflect tests found by the search pass; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t2-test.log. ## Task 3: Drop the haiku workaround from the issue chains Depends on: Task 1 In src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/refs/chains.md remove ` --models opus,sonnet` from the three brainstorm steps in the table rows for Feature simple, Feature medium and Feature complex (lines 11-13), and replace the note at line 21 (the bullet that begins with /sc:brainstorm --models defaults) with a bullet that says: the brainstorm model list defaults to opus,sonnet,haiku and the brainstorm rows use the defaults; in a ccsession tier workspace these aliases map to the tier models once the launcher sets ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL, outside one they keep Claude Code's meaning; see the model-alias reference page in docs/reference. The new bullet must not contain the string `--models`. In tests/skills/test_issue_protocol.py rename test_brainstorm_steps_have_no_handoff_and_pin_models (lines 268-282) to test_brainstorm_steps_have_no_handoff_and_use_default_models and replace `assert "--models opus,sonnet" in step` with an assertion that `--models` is not in the step. In docs/designs/sc-issue-command.md add a note "Superseded by #384: the chains use the default models; see docs/reference/model-aliases.md" to the D25 row (about line 442) and to the bullet at about line 237 that explains the workaround; leave the rest of that design record unchanged. Acceptance criteria: - `grep -n -- "--models" src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/refs/chains.md` returns nothing and the six chain rows still parse (the existing chain tests in tests/skills/test_issue_protocol.py pass). - The chains test of tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py passes; `uv run pytest tests/skills/test_issue_protocol.py tests/skills/test_issue_worker_agents.py` passes; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t3-test.log. ## Task 4: Align the cleanup-audit docs with the audit-scanner pin Depends on: Task 1 src/superclaude/agents/audit-scanner.md pins `model: sonnet` (commit 70ef6486 replaced haiku defaults with sonnet; `git log -S"model: sonnet" -- src/superclaude/agents/audit-scanner.md` returns it); the docs still say Haiku. Leave the agent file unchanged and edit the docs to state Sonnet: in src/superclaude/skills/sc-cleanup-audit-protocol/SKILL.md lines 68 (`audit-scanner` (Haiku)), 74 (Haiku-first cost optimization), 95 (audit-scanner (Haiku, Pass 1)), 99 (Haiku-First Escalation) and 114 (Uses Haiku agents), in src/superclaude/skills/sc-cleanup-audit-protocol/templates/final-report.md line 77 ("Haiku agents"), and in src/superclaude/commands/cleanup-audit.md lines 43 and 53. Replace each Haiku mention with Sonnet or neutral wording (for example "Surface-first escalation: all files get a surface scan, then the flagged subset gets deep analysis"), and remove the 50-70% cost-reduction claim, which was specific to Haiku. Then search src/superclaude and docs/ for any other text that says audit-scanner runs on Haiku and fix it the same way. The Haiku strings in tests/cli_portify/test_discover_components.py are parser fixtures, and the `(Haiku)` comment and regex alternative in src/superclaude/cli/cli_portify/steps/discover_components.py (lines 60 and 121) are parser machinery; both stay. Acceptance criteria: - `grep -rn "Haiku" src/superclaude/skills/sc-cleanup-audit-protocol src/superclaude/commands/cleanup-audit.md` returns nothing and src/superclaude/agents/audit-scanner.md is unchanged. - The cleanup-audit test of tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py passes, and the existing tests that read these files (search tests/ for cleanup-audit and sc-cleanup-audit-protocol) pass; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t4-test.log. ## Task 5: Rename the implement retry-ladder variables to the names the workspace exports Depends on: Task 1 The workspace exports T3Model01, T2Model01, T2Model02, T1Model01 and T1Model02 (no underscore); src/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/refs/retry.md (lines 162-172) names the same variables with an underscore after the tier digit, so the primary ladder never activates. In retry.md replace each underscore name with the exported name (T3Model01, T2Model01, T2Model02, T1Model01, T1Model02) including the tier-token wording at line 164 and the example at line 172, and add one sentence in the Ladders paragraph saying these are the tier slot variables exported by the workspace environment, that T1Model01 and T1Model02 are the legacy Tier 1 slots the workspace keeps for readers such as swarm and reflect, and that the fallback ladder (haiku, sonnet, opus) applies when they are not all set. In src/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/refs/ledger.md change the example tier token at line 200 to `tier=T2Model02`. Copy both edited files over plugins/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/refs/retry.md and plugins/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/refs/ledger.md. In tests/skills/test_workflow_archive.py change the RUNGS entries (lines 774-777) and the tier value in _rt (line 786) to the new names, and in tests/skills/test_task_workspace_lifecycle.py change the assertion at line 597 to the new T2Model01 name. src/superclaude/skills/sc-implement-protocol/scripts/archive_workspace.py already accepts `[A-Za-z0-9_]+` for the tier token and needs no change. Write ./artifacts/t5-notes.md recording the behaviour change: in a workspace that exports the four variables (as /etc/aidev02/aienv.d/defaults.sh does: T3Model01 gpt-6.1-terra, T2Model02 glm-5.3, T1Model02 gpt-6.1-sol, T1Model01 claude-opus-5-5) the primary ladder now replaces the alias fallback ladder; rung 1 is a non-Claude model, rungs 0 and 2 are GPT models, and a claude-sonnet executor sits on no primary rung so its tier is unknown and adviser A takes the top rung. Acceptance criteria: - The retired underscore names no longer appear anywhere in src, plugins, tests or docs (grep for the pattern T[0-4]_Model0 returns nothing), and `cmp` shows the two mirrored files identical to their src counterparts. - ./artifacts/t5-notes.md exists and states the activation and its effect on adviser selection. - The retry names test of tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py passes; `uv run pytest tests/skills/test_workflow_archive.py tests/skills/test_task_workspace_lifecycle.py tests/skills/test_implement_adviser_family.py` passes; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t5-test.log. ## Phase 3: Document the mapping ## Task 6: Write the model-alias reference page Depends on: Task 5 Create docs/reference/model-aliases.md and add a row for it to the "Contracts and design notes" table in docs/reference/README.md. Sections: what a primitive may name (plain aliases only; the issue-worker allow-list and why; the test tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py enforces it); the mapping table (opus to claude-gw-tier1a via ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL, sonnet to claude-gw-tier1b via ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL, haiku to claude-gw-tier2 via ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL inside a ccsession tier workspace; outside one nothing is set and opus, sonnet and haiku keep Claude Code's meaning), stating the mapping is owner-decided on 2026-11-05, is applied by the ccsession launcher in a follow-up change after the #315 pull request merges, and that until then the workspace defaults file exports real model ids for the three variables; why aliases and not picker ids (frontmatter model takes an alias, a full model id or inherit with no environment lookup; the Agent-call model parameter takes only sonnet, opus, haiku and fable; source https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents read 2026-11-05) and the verified behaviour, linking .dev/issues/384/analysis/probe-alias-remap.md (a subagent with model: opus ran on claude-gw-tier1a and one with model: haiku on claude-gw-tier2 while the main session kept its own model; Claude Code logs an unrecognized_model notice for each tier id but serves the request); and a Known consequences section: reflect reviewer diversity counts the three variable values (tier1a and tier1b both list Claude Sonnet 5.5 in src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/MODEL-TIERS.md); the sprint alternate-model suggestion still works when the failed model is given as an alias but returns nothing when it is given as a real model id from a cooldown body while the slots hold tier ids (src/superclaude/cli/sprint/aienv.py lines 111-128); roadmap step ids such as generate-opus-architect and recommend best_model values stay unchanged because the aliases stay; and the implement retry ladder now activates where the four slot variables are set (summarize ./artifacts/t5-notes.md). Acceptance criteria: - docs/reference/model-aliases.md exists with the sections above and the three exports spelled exactly as in the mapping table; docs/reference/README.md links to it. - The mapping document test of tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py passes; `grep -nE "sk-|token=" docs/reference/model-aliases.md` returns nothing; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t6-test.log. ## Task 7: Point the existing model pages at the reference page Depends on: Task 6 Edit src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/refs/tiers.md: in item 4 of the list under "Why the pin lives in frontmatter" (line 26) replace the claim that haiku resolves to glm-5.3 on this workspace with the statement that the haiku alias follows ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL and resolves to claude-gw-tier2 inside a ccsession tier workspace once the launcher sets it; reword the clause at line 40 that says a fallback to haiku can land on a non-Claude model (glm-5.3 here) so it no longer states glm-5.3 as a fixed fact; and add one sentence under "E-TIER-UNAVAILABLE" that the issue workers are the only primitives pinned to picker ids and all other primitives use aliases (docs/reference/model-aliases.md). In docs/user-guide/brainstorm.md extend the `--models` row (line 52) with: in a ccsession tier workspace opus, sonnet and haiku map to claude-gw-tier1a, claude-gw-tier1b and claude-gw-tier2 once the launcher sets them; see docs/reference/model-aliases.md. In docs/user-guide/commands.md add the same pointer to the brainstorm model-selection text around lines 849 and 859. In docs/developer-guide/SuperClaude-Developer-Guide-Commands-Skills-Agents.md edit the agent `model:` description in "4.1 Anatomy of an Agent File" (line 411, which currently says `model:` may be a picker ID such as claude-gw-tier3) so it says `model:` is an alias unless the agent is an allow-listed issue worker, and link docs/reference/model-aliases.md; leave the skills frontmatter section "5.2 SKILL.md Frontmatter" unchanged. Acceptance criteria: - src/superclaude/skills/sc-issue-protocol/refs/tiers.md no longer states glm-5.3 as a fixed fact (the text "glm-5.3 here" is gone), and `uv run pytest tests/skills/test_issue_protocol.py tests/skills/test_issue_worker_agents.py` passes. - docs/user-guide/brainstorm.md, docs/user-guide/commands.md and the developer guide carry the pointer; every added link target exists in the repository; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t7-test.log. ## Phase 4: Guard the launcher follow-up ## Task 8: Add characterization tests for tier-valued alias variables and run the whole policy file Depends on: Task 7 Add tests that pin today's behaviour when the three variables hold tier ids, so the launcher change cannot silently alter it. In tests/sprint/test_aienv.py (existing tests there show the `env=` seam of suggest_alternate_model) assert that with ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-gw-tier1a, ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=claude-gw-tier1b and ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-gw-tier2 the function _load_aliases returns those ids unchanged under the keys opus, sonnet and haiku, that suggest_alternate_model("opus", env=that env) returns "sonnet", and that suggest_alternate_model("claude-opus-5-5", env=that env) returns None (never a fabricated alias). In tests/swarm/test_coder_tier_env_2026_10.py (the module that already tests count_model_aliases, lines 115-124) assert that the same env gives a count of 3. Each test docstring says it records current behaviour and points to the Known consequences section of docs/reference/model-aliases.md. These tests are an optional guard beyond the four listed spec items; keep them small. Acceptance criteria: - The new tests pass on unchanged production code, and `uv run pytest tests/sprint/test_aienv.py tests/swarm/test_coder_tier_env_2026_10.py` passes; evidence saved to ./artifacts/t8-test.log. - `uv run pytest tests/skills/test_model_alias_policy.py` passes in full (all tests green after Tasks 2 to 7), saved to ./artifacts/final-policy.log. ## Task 9: Write the launcher follow-up spec and run its failing-first test Create .dev/issues/384/launcher-followup.md, the exact spec of the separate launcher pull request that may start only after the #315 pull request is merged. Read, without editing, src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/ccsession (the shell launcher), src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/models.py and tests/unit/test_ccsession_tiers.py. The spec states: the file to edit (src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/ccsession) with the anchor, quoted with its line numbers at this branch's base commit and marked "re-verify after #315 merges" (the tier-mode block at lines 776-785, where the launcher also tests that CCSESSION_EXT_PROFILE is not 1 at line 777, and the custom-option exports at lines 1099-1103; PROFILE_MODEL is a shell variable, not an export); the three export lines exactly (export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=claude-gw-tier1a, export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=claude-gw-tier1b, export ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-gw-tier2) and that they run only when tier mode is on, so a launch that is not in tier mode leaves the inherited environment untouched; the tier-mode detection rule from models.py (a T<N>_WINDOW variable exists and CCSESSION_TIERS is not 0, and the launcher's own CCSESSION_EXT_PROFILE check); and a failing-first pytest, as a code block, in the style of the tier-launch tests of tests/unit/test_ccsession_tiers.py using only helpers that exist there. The fake claude in that module records only a fixed set of keys (lines 330-341), so the spec states the exact `json.dump` lines to add to capture ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL, ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL and ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL, and the test removes those three variables from the launch environment first (the harness copies os.environ at line 359, and the workspace exports them). The test asserts the three values in a default tier launch and that a non-tier launch leaves them unset. Run the test: copy the harness and the test into a scratch module under ./artifacts/t9-scratch/ with the harness addition applied, run it with `uv run pytest` against the unchanged launcher, and save the output. Acceptance criteria: - .dev/issues/384/launcher-followup.md exists and contains the file path, the quoted anchor with line numbers, the three exact export lines, the placement and tier-mode rule, the harness addition, the test code block, and the sentence that the edit must not start before the #315 pull request is merged. - ./artifacts/t9-red.log shows the scratch test failing with an AssertionError on the three variable values (not a KeyError and not an import error), and every helper name used in the test code block exists in tests/unit/test_ccsession_tiers.py (checked by grep and listed in the spec file). - No file under src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/ was modified (`git diff --stat -- src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag` is empty).